From b1dfc2ba819e4001fb9d91c021e54fc10d7f4151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akif-b-Atif <akif.b.atif@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:50:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add chain detection to the chat analyzer reports

Ports the standalone find_chains.py into the analyzer (chains.py): finds the
longest runs where a message or a cycle of messages repeats back to back,
tolerating case, punctuation and a one-character typo. Every message is
compared against the original pattern so fuzzy matches can't drift, and the
walk also extends backwards to catch chains whose first cycle was interrupted.

A single unrelated message inside a chain doesn't break it (CHAIN_TOLERANCE,
default 1); media/deleted/call placeholders count as such interruptions.
Interruptions are reported per chain and not counted in its length.

It works on the analyzer's dataframe (system rows skipped), takes its
tunables from CHAIN_* in chat_config instead of module globals, and adds a
Chains section to the HTML and PDF reports for the main report, the
last-N-days part and every arc, selectable with --sections chains. Includes
tests (among them a differential test against the original algorithm) and
docs.
